--- /dev/null
+++ b/PROGRESS.md
@@ -0,0 +1,34 @@
+# Experiment: multiple datoms per SlateDB key (row-major segments)
+
+## Goal
+Datomic-style segments: up to N sorted datom keys under one key (keyed by the last datom key), per-datom encoding unchanged. Isolate the effect of key count / per-key LSM overhead. Toggle: TRIPLOX_SEGMENT_SIZE (1 = today's layout; measure 64, 256, 1024). Readers accept both layouts in one index. Point lookups, lookup refs, temporal filtering, CDC must keep working.
+
+## Status (as of hand-off)
+- Compiles (cargo check --all-targets clean). Previous agent reported "Build passes" after porting the three iterators onto a segment cursor.
+- New: src/segment.rs (layout, configured_segment_size, cursor, write helpers).
+- Modified: benches/datalog_bench.rs, bootstrap.rs, incremental/cdc.rs, indexer.rs, iterator/{slate_iterator,slate_key_iterator,temporal_filter_iterator}.rs, lib.rs, node.rs, query/patterns/triple.rs, tempids.rs, tx.rs.
+- Previous agent's stated next steps: a public storage-stats hook for the bench (key count / bytes per index), the cross-size equivalence test, and bench output for storage numbers.
+
+## Next
+1. Run bench with TRIPLOX_SEGMENT_SIZE=256 and check row counts against baseline. Fix correctness first.
+2. Storage-stats hook + bench output; equivalence test across sizes including an as-of query.
+3. cargo test -p triplox (with default size 1 and with 256), clippy.
+4. A/B bench (size 1 vs best size, 3 each alternating) plus one run at each other size.
+5. EXPERIMENT.md (mention the 65 KiB key limit and CDC), fmt, commit.
+
+## Shared context
+
+Toolchain: every shell needs `export PATH="$HOME/.rustup/toolchains/1.95.0-aarch64-apple-darwin/bin:$PATH"` and `export CARGO_BUILD_JOBS=3`. Never run `cargo clean`. Work only in this worktree.
+
+Benchmark: `cargo bench --bench datalog_bench` (env VERTICES, EDGE_PROB, RUNS, BENCH_OUT). Baseline JSON: /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-ben-code-triplox/2cc95019-6318-4527-8430-7ad4b12972b9/scratchpad/results/baseline.json. Baseline medians (ms): triangles 537 (7821 rows), two_hop_count 223, three_hop_count 7041, out_degree 44 (2000 rows), in_degree_top 44 (2000 rows), neighbors_of_42 1.1 (21 rows), weight_filter 3.7 (198 rows), weight_sum 3.6, heavy_neighbors 68 (1908 rows), label_lookup 0.02 (1 row).
+
+Definition of done:
+1. Feature behind an env toggle; results identical on/off (row counts match baseline; an on/off equivalence test on a small graph).
+2. `cargo test -p triplox` and `cargo clippy -p triplox --all-targets` pass, or failures are listed here honestly.
+3. A/B interleaved bench, 3 runs each; JSON written to /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-ben-code-triplox/2cc95019-6318-4527-8430-7ad4b12972b9/scratchpad/results/datom-segments-off.json and /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-ben-code-triplox/2cc95019-6318-4527-8430-7ad4b12972b9/scratchpad/results/datom-segments-on.json.
+4. EXPERIMENT.md at worktree root: what was built, hook points (file:line), A/B table, what failed, honest verdict and integration cost.
+5. `cargo fmt`; commit on this branch; do not push; no GitHub issues/PRs.
+
+## Progress protocol
+
+After every milestone (compiles, test passes, bench run, doc written): update the Status and Next sections below, then `git add -A && git commit -q -m "wip(datom-segments): <milestone>"`. Commit even if incomplete. This file is the hand-off; a fresh agent must be able to continue from it alone.
